% Blind extraction: the editor's "facts from a document" path (docs/le_summary.md
% §17.9, nl_to_le:english_to_le/8) run headless on ten Medicare Appeals Council
% decisions already transcribed by hand (council_pmd.le, council_other.le,
% council_more.le), 13 September 2026, with two open-weight models:
% openai/gpt-oss-120b on Groq (scenarios blind_gpt_...) and moonshotai/Kimi-K3
% on Together (blind_kimi_..., with a 60,000-token budget: Kimi thinks before
% it writes). The program offered to the model was the one policy the
% decision concerns (pmd, nebulizers, aeds, hospital_beds, glucose_monitors):
% its scenario templates and the values its rules read. The facts are the
% models' own, UNEDITED — codes left unquoted, passages paraphrased, as they
% came back. README.md ("Blind extraction") compares them with the hand
% transcriptions.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base blind extraction includes these resources:
    pmd,
    nebulizers,
    aeds,
    hospital_beds,
    glucose_monitors.

